  "details": "I know this was already suggested but I'll explain it in a tiny bit better way than the previous guy did.\n\nInstead of making a world private when you update it the currently public and approved one shouldn't be set to private but be available as long as the new one is still private. When the update gets approved the earlier version should be overwritten.\nI know this wouldn't work with the current world ID system, maybe private worlds should have an additional string at the end of the already existing world ID to mark them different, as example \"priv\" at the end of the world string so people who still want to join can join the private one too without changing the whole world ID to a new one.",
